DadaSafe Dashboard

DadaSafe is a digital safety platform designed to educate young women in Kenya about digital safety, online risks, and responsible digital practices. The platform also provides a support pathway for users who have experienced cyberbullying or other technology-related challenges by connecting them with mental health and support providers.

The DadaSafe Dashboard is the web-based management interface used to manage and support these services. It consists of two main dashboard environments: the Admin Dashboard and the Support Provider Dashboard. Both dashboards are built within the same frontend application and are separated using Next.js routing, allowing each authorized user type to access the tools relevant to their role.

The Admin Dashboard is designed for administrators responsible for managing the platform and its educational content. It provides access to platform statistics, user management, administrative settings, game generation, topic and theme selection, AI-assisted game creation, game previews, and JSON payload management. Administrators can also perform actions such as suspending or banning users and monitoring support-related information.

The Support Provider Dashboard is designed for authorized support providers who manage support requests submitted through the platform. Providers can view incoming requests, see the user's email and optional phone number, review the problem description, view the submission date, search through cases, and update the status and priority of requests. The dashboard uses the statuses pending, in_progress, and attended in the user interface, where attended represents the backend's resolved status.

The application is built using Next.js and React, with JavaScript/JSX used for application logic and component development. Tailwind CSS and custom CSS are used for the dashboard layouts and styling, while Lucide React provides interface icons and TanStack Form is used for form management. The frontend communicates with the DadaSafe FastAPI backend through RESTful API endpoints using the browser Fetch API. The backend handles authentication, authorization, database operations, user information, support requests, and game data, while the dashboard provides the interface through which authorized users interact with these services.

The overall application structure can be represented as:

DadaSafe Dashboard
│
├── Admin Dashboard
│   ├── Dashboard
│   ├── Settings
│   ├── User Management
│   ├── Game Management
│   ├── AI Game Generation
│   ├── Topic Selection
│   ├── Game Preview
│   └── JSON Editor
│
└── Support Provider Dashboard
    ├── Dashboard
    ├── Support Requests
    ├── Case Statistics
    ├── Case Search
    ├── Status Management
    ├── Priority Management
    ├── Profile
    └── Settings

Example routes include:

/admin/dashboard
/admin/settings
/admin/control

/support/dashboard
/support/profile

The dashboard follows a component-based architecture, allowing individual features such as sidebars, forms, tables, game previews, topic selectors, and JSON editors to be developed and maintained independently. This structure makes the application easier to extend as additional administrative and support functionality is introduced.

Overall, the DadaSafe Dashboard provides a centralized, role-based web interface that connects the platform's administrators and support providers to the core DadaSafe services. By combining educational game management with support-request management, the dashboard helps ensure that both the learning and support sides of the DadaSafe platform can be managed efficiently from a single application.
